# AFK harness scratch (run-implements-*.ps1). Everything the runner writes is a machine
# artifact of one night's run — session transcripts (~2 MB of JSONL each), the system
# prompts it fed them, stderr and the dev-server logs the slices started. Regenerated by
# re-running, worthless to read, and 58 MB of it accumulated over four waves.
#
# Two deliberate exceptions, in opposite directions:
#   * HITL-<ticket>.md — the decisions a session took with nobody to ask. The tickets LINK
#     these ("four calls in .afk/HITL-238.md"), so they are committed on purpose.
#   * REVIEW-<ticket>.md — written fresh by each wave's round-B reviewer. Deliberately NOT
#     tracked even though it is prose: a tracked one makes the reviewer's own write look
#     like "the reviewer edited the tree", which is a stop condition in the runner. Its
#     findings reach the repo through the ticket's Answer, not through the file.
.afk/*
!.afk/HITL-*.md

